WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.235
Ground an answer in evidence.

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:05.364
Retrieval gives a model relevant source passages.

00:00:05.364 --> 00:00:11.623
Keep each passage linked to its document so the answer can cite its evidence.

00:00:11.623 --> 00:00:14.305
Find passages related to the question.

00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:16.987
Include those passages with the request.

00:00:16.987 --> 00:00:20.116
Check each answer against its cited passage.

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:22.075
Choose retrieval chunks.

00:00:22.075 --> 00:00:26.299
A useful chunk contains enough context to stand alone.

00:00:26.299 --> 00:00:31.461
Preserve headings and document identifiers as you divide a long source.

00:00:31.461 --> 00:00:34.277
Split around headings and topic changes.

00:00:34.277 --> 00:00:37.562
Carry the section title with each passage.

00:00:37.562 --> 00:00:40.848
Store the source ID and page number.

00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:43.264
Evaluate a retrieval result.

00:00:43.264 --> 00:00:48.090
Use a small set of questions with known supporting sources.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:52.917
Check what the retriever returns before changing the model prompt.

00:00:52.917 --> 00:00:56.295
Record one supporting source for each question.

00:00:56.295 --> 00:00:58.226
Inspect the highest-ranked passages.

00:00:58.226 --> 00:01:01.604
Count questions with a relevant top result.

